You, the One enthroned in heaven.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"Do you not know? Have you not heard? The LORD is the everlasting God, the Creator of the ends of the earth. He will not grow tired or weary; His understanding is beyond searching out.","from":2},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":44,"source":"openbible","text":"He gives power to the faint and increases the strength of the weak.","from":2},{"book":"PRO","chapter":3,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":39,"source":"both","text":"for the LORD will be your confidence and will keep your foot from the snare.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-8":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H8104","lemma":"שָׁמַר","tr":"sha·mar","gloss":"to keep: obey","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":469},{"base":"H3394","lemma":"יָרֵחַ","tr":"ya·re·ach","gloss":"moon","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":27},{"base":"H6738","lemma":"צֵל","tr":"tsel","gloss":"shadow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":49},{"base":"H3119","lemma":"יוֹמָם","tr":"yo·mam","gloss":"by day","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":50},{"base":"H8121","lemma":"שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ","tr":"she·mesh","gloss":"sun","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":134},{"base":"H3225","lemma":"יָמִין","tr":"ya·min","gloss":"right","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":140},{"base":"H3915","lemma":"לַ֫יְלָה","tr":"lay·lah","gloss":"night","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":233},{"base":"H6258","lemma":"עַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"now","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":433},{"base":"H5769","lemma":"עוֹלָם","tr":"o·lam","gloss":"forever: enduring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":438},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":500}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":34,"source":"both","text":"You will be blessed when you come in and blessed when you go out.","from":8},{"book":"PSA","chapter":91,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"Because you have made the LORD your dwelling— my refuge, the Most High—","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":91,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"They will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.","from":7},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":28,"source":"both","text":"And the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring me safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":41,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will protect and preserve him; He will bless him in the land and refuse to give him over to the will of his foes.","from":7},{"book":"PRO","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"to guard the paths of justice and protect the way of His saints.","from":8},{"book":"ISA","chapter":25,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"For You have been a refuge for the poor, a stronghold for the needy in distress, a refuge from the storm, a shade from the heat. For the breath of the ruthless is like rain against a wall,","from":5},{"book":"REV","chapter":7,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"‘Never again will they hunger, and never will they thirst; nor will the sun beat down upon them, nor any scorching heat.’","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}